I am not supper convinced about this, as this requiers to also change the rpc `listtransaction` and may difficult things in the future if some new parameters are introduced in one of the rpcs. Just wanted to comment the idea to see what others think.

-<ins>_**Updates**_</ins>:
- Addressed @Bicaru20's [feedback](https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/35813#pullrequestreview-4863711017):
  - Split the first commit into two — now 3 commits: RPC implementation, functional test, and release notes;
  - `ListRawTransaction` now pushes to `ret` directly via [template](https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/35813#discussion_r3727812567) `<class Vec>` (matching `ListTransactions` style), with a verbose param added for the decoded output;
  - [Removed](https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/35813#discussion_r3720042023) `listtransactions` API calls from `test_one_entry_per_tx` and `test_consolidation_tx_visible`; kept explanatory comments documenting why the comparison matters conceptually;
  - [Replaced](https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/35813#discussion_r3720095605) bare `assert` comparisons with `assert_greater_than` and `assert_greater_than_or_equal`;
  - On the shared `ListTransactionHelper` suggestion: `listtransactions` and `listrawtransactions` have fundamentally different semantics — the former works per-output with category assignment, label filtering, and change suppression; the latter works per-transaction with no categorisation. A shared raw flag would couple two RPCs that are likely to diverge further (e.g. the new verbose param only applies to `listrawtransactions`). Keeping them independent is cleaner.
- Addressed @achow101's [feedback](https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/35813#pullrequestreview-4900868755):
  - Added verbose (`bool`, default `false`); `hex` is always included in the output; `decoded` is added when `verbose=true` (matches the `gettransaction` pattern);
  - Removed `category` field references from `TransactionDescriptionString()` help strings — descriptions no longer reference the `category` field;
  - [Variables](https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/35813#discussion_r3753287085) are now snake_case;
  - [Using](https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/35813#discussion_r3753304625) `self.Arg<int>("count")`, `self.Arg<int>("skip")`, `self.Arg<bool>("verbose")`;
  - Pagination now [skips](https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/35813#discussion_r3753420417) in the loop directly; result assembled with `result.push_backV(ret.rbegin(), ret.rend())`.

There is some code duplications between `listtransactions` and `listrawtransaction` some static helper function would probably make it more clean and readable.

